// spec: a brace list with more values than its array takes is an error, as in C++ ([dcl.init.aggr] 9: `int a[2] = {1, 2, 3}`), and so it is where an element's braces are elided (`In b[1] = {1, 2, 3}`: {1, 2} takes two)
// found by thread D (2026-11-06): codegen dropped the values past the array's end without a word (`int a[2] = {1, 2, 3}` printed 1 2)
// error: array_with_more_values_than_elements_is_error.kpp:6: error: more values than an array of 2 int32 takes
int main()
{
  int a[2] = {1, 2, 3};
  std::println(a[0], " ", a[1]);
  return 0;
}
